  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Given that $\\cos\\theta=\\frac{1}{3}$, find $\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\displaystyle \\pm\\frac{\\sqrt6}{3}$.\n\nThe sign depends on the quadrant of $\\frac{\\theta}{2}$, which is not specified.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}&=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\cos\\theta}{2}}\\\\\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}&=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{1+\\frac13}{2}}\\\\\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}&=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac23}\\\\\\cos\\frac{\\theta}{2}&=\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt6}{3}\\end{align*}$$\n\nNo interval for $\\theta$ is given, so either sign is possible.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
  },
